#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# frobenius_solve

#% text
# `frobenius_solve(coins, k)` gives all lists of non-negative integers `x` with `coins.x = k`, in increasing lexicographic order; `frobenius_solve(coins, k, m)` at most `m` of them.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
frobenius_solve([6, 9, 20], 44)
#% output
#= [[1, 2, 1], [4, 0, 1]]

#% cell
frobenius_solve([6, 9, 20], 44, 1)
#% output
#= [[1, 2, 1]]

#% cell
frobenius_solve([5, 2, 1], 3)
#% output
#= [[0, 0, 3], [0, 1, 1]]

#% cell
frobenius_solve([6, 9, 20], 43)
#% output
#= []

